{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 18:57:28.438865", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### Network Description\\nThe network is an SDN star topology with one central switch (switch_0) and multiple edge switches (switch_1, switch_2, switch_3, switch_4). Hosts (host_1, host_2, host_3, host_4) are connected to edge switches, and all devices share a single access subnet (10.0.0.0/24). The SDN controller operates at 20.0.0.100 and manages the switches via OpenFlow.\\n\\n#### Observations\\n1. **Reachability Test Results**:\\n   - **host_1 to host_3**: Status is `unknown`. No packets were transmitted or received, and no RTT data is available.\\n   - **host_2 to host_3**: Status is `ok`. Packets were successfully transmitted and received with 0% loss. RTT average is 9.662 ms.\\n   - **host_2 to host_1**: Status is `unknown`. No packets were transmitted or received, and no RTT data is available.\\n   - **host_3 to host_1**: Status is `unknown`. No packets were transmitted or received, and no RTT data is available.\\n   - **host_4 to host_3**: Status is `ok`. Packets were successfully transmitted and received with 0% loss. RTT average is 7.124 ms.\\n   - **host_4 to host_1**: Status is `unknown`. No packets were transmitted or received, and no RTT data is available.\\n\\n2. **Anomalies Detected**:\\n   - Multiple reachability tests resulted in a status of `unknown`, indicating potential connectivity issues between certain hosts.\\n   - Specifically, host_1 appears to be unreachable from host_2, host_3, and host_4.\\n   - Host_3 and host_4 are reachable from host_2 and host_4, respectively, suggesting partial connectivity within the network.\\n\\n#### Findings\\n- **Host Connectivity**:\\n  - Host_1 seems to be isolated or experiencing network issues, as it is unreachable from other hosts.\\n  - Host_3 and host_4 exhibit normal connectivity with host_2 and host_4, respectively.\\n\\n- **Potential Root Cause**:\\n  - The issue may stem from the edge switch (switch_1) connected to host_1 or the central switch (switch_0) responsible for routing traffic between edge switches.\\n  - Alternatively, there could be a misconfiguration or failure in the SDN controller affecting OpenFlow rules for host_1.\\n\\n#### Next Steps\\nFurther investigation is required to pinpoint the root cause of the connectivity issues. This includes examining the network configuration of host_1 and its associated switch (switch_1), as well as verifying the OpenFlow rules and SDN controller status., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='da1c0cdf-a1b5-4c00-99e7-930378d6d03d'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
